Test vectors
------------

Tests use the worked examples and test values of the standards as facts:
the IEC 62056-46 annex A FCS table values and example frames, the ISO/IEC
13239:2002 bit layouts, the IEC 62056-4-7 annex A.4 segmented WPDU, the
IEC 62056-5-3:2023 annex E ciphered release, the IEC 62056-6-1:2023 and
EN 13757-1:2021 examples and minimum objects, the IEC 62056-5-3:2023
Table 30 and annex E ciphering examples and the DLMS UA Green Book's AES-GCM
example. cosem's tests also use the RFC 3394 key wrap examples and NIST
CAVS 11.0 ECDSA SigVer vectors (public domain, as shipped in the Go
source tree). Keys in examples and tests are test values, not keys of
any meter.

The test-only module interop/ (not part of the published module) fetches
Gurux's GPL-2.0 sources and unit-test vectors (Gurux.DLMS.Java,
Gurux.DLMS.Android) and the gurux-dlms Python package when its tests run,
to check this module against them; none of them is kept or redistributed.
Its testdata/gurux_client.py is our own script that calls that package.

